{
  "format": "memory-admin-routes/1",
  "$comment": [
    "Route classes of the admin listener. Final: every route of the admin listener application is listed here, and the other way round. Read by gateway/src/admin-plane/registry.ts; checked by the maintainers' contract checks.",
    "class: read — GET and POST without changes; narrow — narrowing, allowed in break-glass; ordinary — one administrator, not in break-glass; second_signature — second signature always; conditional — second signature if the condition is true; test_only — 404 without MEMORY_TEST_HOOKS=1; removed — always 404 or 400; auth — sign-in, no session.",
    "roles: which session roles may use the route (memory_admin, security_auditor); a system key and a mem_adm_ session count as memory_admin. breakglass: whether an emergency-access session is allowed. approvers: roles of the signers (both by default).",
    "path — as in Hono (:param); OpenAPI writes {param}. One line per route: edits of separate parts merge without conflicts."
  ],
  "classes": ["read", "narrow", "ordinary", "second_signature", "conditional", "test_only", "removed", "auth"],
  "roles": ["memory_admin", "security_auditor"],
  "routes": [
    {"id": "admin.models.get", "method": "GET", "path": "/api/v1/admin/models", "class": "read", "roles": ["memory_admin"], "breakglass": true, "note": "Resolved model roles; credentials represented only by a constant mask. Settings saves use the existing guarded settings route."},
    {"id": "admin.models.presets.get", "method": "GET", "path": "/api/v1/admin/models/presets", "class": "read", "roles": ["memory_admin"], "breakglass": true},
    {"id": "admin.models.test.post", "method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/admin/models/test", "class": "ordinary", "roles": ["memory_admin"], "breakglass": false, "note": "Built-in synthetic probe outside the data-policy gate (audited as data_policy_bypassed), through the common request builder, destination checks and chat slot. Unknown fields are refused; inherited keys and wire options stay on their origin. Results grant no permission and expose only codes and bounded facts, never upstream detail or credentials. Candidate outcomes do not change the shared breaker or dirty-slot hold."},
    {"id": "admin.models.usage.get", "method": "GET", "path": "/api/v1/admin/models/usage", "class": "read", "roles": ["memory_admin"], "breakglass": true},
    {"id": "first_run.get", "method": "GET", "path": "/api/v1/first-run", "class": "auth", "roles": [], "breakglass": false, "note": "First-run setup: needed — only while there are no admin_users and nobody has memory_admin; first_admin_needed — while nobody has memory_admin (tools/admin/first-admin.mjs)"},
    {"id": "first_run.post", "method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/first-run", "class": "auth", "roles": [], "breakglass": false, "note": "admin@local — while there are no admin_users and nobody has memory_admin; with admin.system_key_admin=false no system key is created. Body {code, person} — the first memory administrator, from a profile with a confirmed directory (AD) link (tools/admin/first-admin.mjs), only with the installation code and only while nobody has memory_admin"},
    {"id": "admin_login.post", "method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/admin-login", "class": "auth", "roles": [], "breakglass": false, "note": "admin@local by admin.local_login: open — as before (on the separate admin listener — a mem_as_ session, auth_method local); breakglass — only while an emergency-access window is open (local_breakglass, expiry no later than the window); off — 404"},
    {"id": "admin_auth.local_totp.get", "method": "GET", "path": "/api/v1/admin/local-totp", "class": "read", "roles": ["memory_admin"], "breakglass": true, "note": "own second factor of a local administrator (session local / local_breakglass or a legacy mem_adm_ token); everyone else gets 404"},
    {"id": "admin_auth.local_totp.enroll.post", "method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/admin/local-totp/enroll", "class": "ordinary", "roles": ["memory_admin"], "breakglass": true, "note": "the password again, inside the sign-in brute-force window; pending secret for 10 minutes"},
    {"id": "admin_auth.local_totp.confirm.post", "method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/admin/local-totp/confirm", "class": "ordinary", "roles": ["memory_admin"], "breakglass": true, "note": "first code switches the factor on; 10 recovery codes once; other sessions of the login revoked"},
    {"id": "admin_auth.local_totp.disable.post", "method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/admin/local-totp/disable", "class": "ordinary", "roles": ["memory_admin"], "breakglass": true, "note": "a TOTP or recovery code switches the factor off; refused while admin.local_totp_required"},
    {"id": "admin_auth.totp.reset.post", "method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/admin-auth/totp/reset", "class": "auth", "roles": [], "breakglass": false, "note": "console reset only (unix socket of the admin listener or loopback without any forwarding header), with the install code; otherwise 404"},
    {"id": "health.get", "method": "GET", "path": "/api/v1/health", "class": "auth", "roles": [], "breakglass": true, "note": "Health without a session — status only; details go to an administrator session"},
