    {"id": "admin.people.id.factor.reset.post", "method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/admin/people/:id/factor/reset", "class": "second_signature", "roles": ["memory_admin"], "breakglass": false, "always": true, "action": "mfa.factor_reset", "subject_param": "id", "note": "Second factor route (factor-admin.ts). Action mfa.factor_reset: in advanced — a second signature always; in basic — immediately, but only with a person’s own session (otherwise 403 human_session_required); the basic_auto decision is set by approval_basic_auto. The body {reason, identity_confirmed, manager_confirmed} is checked before the request: a malformed id, a nonexistent profile and an incomplete body create no request in any mode; when a signed request is executed, the handler checks the body once more; the request summary is the employee’s login and both marks. The request is bound to the person :id — authcheck consumes it: approval_consume(id, 'mfa.factor_reset', sha256('mfa.factor_reset' ‖ '\\n' ‖ person_id)) (T2)"},
